00:30:05.170 --> 00:30:06.840
- [Priya] Chris.

00:30:06.840 --> 00:30:08.776
- Yeah, so very curious,

00:30:08.776 --> 00:30:10.680
I know you didn't have a chance

00:30:10.680 --> 00:30:11.790
to go into a lot of the details,

00:30:11.790 --> 00:30:12.990
but I was curious about exactly

00:30:12.990 --> 00:30:15.780
what the isomorphic
structures are that you're,

00:30:15.780 --> 00:30:18.120
so if they're both just Hilbert spaces,

00:30:18.120 --> 00:30:21.360
there's one sense in
which it could be trivial,

00:30:21.360 --> 00:30:23.370
but there might be more
structures on the Hilbert space

00:30:23.370 --> 00:30:24.840
that you're mapping into in another.

00:30:24.840 --> 00:30:27.900
And similar to Dave's question,
I was wondering just like,

00:30:27.900 --> 00:30:30.330
you know, think of the
standard properties,

00:30:30.330 --> 00:30:31.650
you think of the quantum vacuum,

00:30:31.650 --> 00:30:33.540
like the Reeh-Schlieder theorem.

00:30:33.540 --> 00:30:37.253
How is that modeled in CM+?

00:30:38.130 --> 00:30:39.650
- What you can do is you,

00:30:39.650 --> 00:30:43.418
if you construct the quantum field,

00:30:43.418 --> 00:30:45.330
the electromagnetic quantum field theory

00:30:45.330 --> 00:30:48.813
in terms of creation and
annihilation operators,

00:30:49.789 --> 00:30:53.610
then there's an involution
that you can construct,

00:30:53.610 --> 00:30:55.200
which allows you to construct in terms of

00:30:55.200 --> 00:30:57.870
the same creation of
organization operators,

00:30:57.870 --> 00:31:00.240
an operator that commutes everywhere.

00:31:00.240 --> 00:31:03.867
So instead of the f measurement
and the g measurement,

00:31:03.867 --> 00:31:07.590
the commutator being a
function of the f and g,

00:31:07.590 --> 00:31:09.780
a linear function of the f and g,

00:31:09.780 --> 00:31:11.670
instead of that, you
find that the commutator

00:31:11.670 --> 00:31:15.213
of this new f measurement
and g measurement is zero.

00:31:16.170 --> 00:31:18.240
So the involution does the job,

00:31:18.240 --> 00:31:23.240
but the involution has
a time reversal in it.

00:31:24.300 --> 00:31:25.953
And that's non-local.

00:31:27.150 --> 00:31:31.560
So it's a very, very simple construction.

00:31:31.560 --> 00:31:33.330
If I was giving an hour-long court talk,

00:31:33.330 --> 00:31:36.929
then it would be in
there, and in one slide.

00:31:36.929 --> 00:31:39.990
It's quite simple, but anyway.

00:31:39.990 --> 00:31:41.760
- [Priya] did you have a quick follow up?

00:31:41.760 --> 00:31:43.020
- [Chris] Well, so I
still don't understand

00:31:43.020 --> 00:31:46.260
